<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="MauiReference.Pages.GapEventAttributePage" Title="Gap: Event Attribute">
    <!-- P3 gap probe: an inline event attribute (Clicked="..."). AUTHORING.md rule 3 bans these in
         shared/tier-1 pages because the port hydrates a static tree with no event-attribute support; this
         tier-2 gap page pins that exact limitation deliberately, per rule 6. Verified: xaml_loader::
         load_into throws "Cannot assign property 'Clicked': Property does not exist" — Clicked is
         rejected as an unrecognized property, not silently ignored. NOTE: e2e.py lint's EVENT_RE
         regex-rejects this attribute name UNCONDITIONALLY for every page under pages/ (it has no tier-2
         carve-out), so this file intentionally is NOT run through `e2e.py gen`/`lint` — see this gap's
         manifest.json row (notes) for how it's verified instead. GapEventAttributePage.xaml.cs is
         hand-written (has OnClicked) so real MAUI still renders + behaves correctly (the acceptance
         gate). -->
    <VerticalStackLayout Margin="12" Spacing="8">
        <Label Text="Gap probe: Clicked=&quot;OnClicked&quot; event attribute" />
        <Button Text="Click me" Clicked="OnClicked" />
    </VerticalStackLayout>
</ContentPage>
